  52:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) Start the FDCAN module using HAL_FDCAN_Start function. At this level
  53:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           the node is active on the bus: it can send and receive messages.
  54:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  55:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) The following Tx control functions can only be called when the FDCAN
  56:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           module is started:
  57:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_AddMessageToTxFifoQ
  58:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****             (++) HAL_FDCAN_AbortTxRequest
  59:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  60:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) After having submitted a Tx request in Tx Fifo or Queue, it is possible to
  61:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           get Tx buffer location used to place the Tx request thanks to
  62:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           HAL_FDCAN_GetLatestTxFifoQRequestBuffer API.
  63:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           It is then possible to abort later on the corresponding Tx Request using
  64:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           HAL_FDCAN_AbortTxRequest API.
  65:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  66:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) When a message is received into the FDCAN message RAM, it can be
  67:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           retrieved using the HAL_FDCAN_GetRxMessage function.
  68:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  69:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) Calling the HAL_FDCAN_Stop function stops the FDCAN module by entering
  70:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           it to initialization mode and re-enabling access to configuration
  71:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           registers through the configuration functions listed here above.
  72:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
  73:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****       (#) All other control functions can be called any time after initialization
  74:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c ****           phase, no matter if the FDCAN module is started or stopped.
  75:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_fdcan.c **** 
